### Courier Platform — manual API walkthrough
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (by Huachao Mao).
### Click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom — tokens/ids
### captured from one response are reused automatically in later requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### 1. Register a company + its first admin
# @name registerCompany
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register-company
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyName": "Acme Delivery",
  "adminEmail": "admin@acme.test",
  "adminFullName": "Admin User",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123"
}

### 2. Log in as the admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123"
}

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. View my company
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Onboard a courier (creates User + Vehicle + Courier together)
# @name onboardCourier
POST {{baseUrl}}/couriers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "courier1@acme.test",
  "fullName": "Aziz Kuryer",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123",
  "vehicleType": "BICYCLE",
  "plateNumber": null
}

@courierId = {{onboardCourier.response.body.id}}

### 5. List couriers (should show the one just onboarded)
GET {{baseUrl}}/couriers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Log in as the courier
# @name loginCourier
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "courier1@acme.test",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123"
}

@courierToken = {{loginCourier.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Courier views their own profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/couriers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### 8. Courier sets their own status to AVAILABLE
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/couriers/me/status
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### 9. Register a navigation device
# @name registerDevice
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hardwareId": "DEV-0001"
}

@deviceId = {{registerDevice.response.body.id}}

### 10. Pair the device to the courier (note the pairingToken — shown only once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices/{{deviceId}}/pair
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courierId": "{{courierId}}"
}

### 11. Create an order (Tashkent coordinates)
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pickupAddress": "EVOS, Amir Temur ko'chasi",
  "pickup": { "lat": 41.311081, "lng": 69.240562 },
  "deliveryAddress": "Customer address, Chilonzor",
  "delivery": { "lat": 41.32993, "lng": 69.267294 },
  "customerName": "Customer Name",
  "customerPhone": "+998901234567"
}

@orderId = {{createOrder.response.body.id}}

### Sanity check: does the returned pickup/delivery match what you sent? (This is the part worth double-checking first — see README.)

### 12. Assign the order to the courier
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courierId": "{{courierId}}"
}

### 13. Courier accepts the order (courier.status should flip to DELIVERING — check step 14)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toStatus": "ACCEPTED"
}

### 14. Confirm courier status flipped to DELIVERING
GET {{baseUrl}}/couriers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### 15. Advance through the rest of the lifecycle, one call per step:
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatus": "PICKUP" }

### 16.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatus": "PICKED_UP" }

### 17.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatus": "DELIVERING" }

### 18.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatus": "DELIVERED" }

### 19. Confirm courier status is back to AVAILABLE
GET {{baseUrl}}/couriers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
